==English==

===Etymology===
Apparently a plural form of {{m|en|taw}}, though attested earlier.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/tɔːz/}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɔːz}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|chiefly|Scotland}} A [[leather]] [[strap]] or [[thong]] which is [[split#Verb|split]] into (typically [[three]]) [[tail#Noun|tails]], used for [[corporal punishment]] in [[school#Noun|schools]], [[apply|applied]] to the [[palm#Noun|palm]] of the [[hand#Noun|hands]] or [[buttock]]s.
#* {{RQ:Yeats Wild Swans|year=1919|poem=The Saint and the Hunchback|pages=104–105|pageref=104|passage=I lay about me with the '''taws''' / That night and morning I may thrash / Greek Alexander from my flesh, [...]}}

====Alternative forms====
* {{l|en|taws}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive|chiefly|Scotland}} To [[beat#Verb|beat]] with a [[#Noun|tawse]].

